## Stretch: aggregation preview

Counting likes per post without N+1 (this comes up constantly):

```python
from django.db.models import Count

posts = Post.objects.annotate(like_count=Count("likes")).order_by("-like_count")
for p in posts:
    print(p.title, p.like_count)
```

`annotate` adds a computed column to each row, computed in SQL.

